  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Objective**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the user\'s request. It seems they need a tool that allows them to create and manage multi-page documents. Each page should accommodate both images and text, culminating in a PDF output. My immediate task is to clearly define this functionality to clarify the system requirements.\n\n\n**Refining the Specification**\n\nI\'m now incorporating detailed specifications for a PDF portfolio builder. It needs to be user-friendly, with the ability to add images and text to individual pages, as well as easy page reordering. Global formatting options are crucial, including various layout templates and page orientation choices. Furthermore, I\'m considering text editing features, high-quality output, and English font support for a professional look.\n\n\n**Expanding Design Scope**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific design elements and user experience. I\'ve been brainstorming potential templates, including a case study layout, a biography design, and a four-image grid with captions, but I\'d like to provide users with fully flexible, customizable blocks, or even a free-form editing canvas. Clarity and intuitiveness are paramount. I\'m also considering the user\'s need for a wide selection of English fonts, potentially incorporating a variety of Google Fonts.\n\n\n\n**Prioritizing Output Quality**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on high-quality PDF exports. My focus is ensuring crisp, high-DPI outputs using `jspdf` with high-DPI HTML5 canvas rendering or `html-to-image` plus `jspdf`, but also a native vector option. It\'s crucial to offer selectable DPI options for export, ranging from standard to print master quality. I\'ll consider how these specifications fit into a \'Phase 1\' protocol for image generation. To start, I\'ll batch-generate a set of architectural images to provide a professional portfolio starting point.\n\n\n"
